4. THE ONE TEST THAT CHANGED TO GET HERE, AND WHY IT IS NOT A WEAKENING
===============================================================================

At the first gate run on f7bce1b this suite was 135/136. The single failure:

  Failed Backup_Succeeds_WritesDumpWithChecksumThatVerifies [666 ms]
  Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Succeeded>. Actual:<Partial>.
  Backup did not succeed. Detail: Dump written and verified, but the
  off-host copy did not happen: no ready volume labelled 'MERCHBACKUP'
  is attached. The local dump is the only copy.

That test's own <summary> states its subject: "a run produces a dump, records
its size and checksum, and the checksum recomputed from the file on disk
matches what was recorded." It died on its FIRST assertion, before reaching
any of the checksum assertions that are its purpose.

The change (229748e): accept Succeeded OR Partial; Failed still fails. Both
of the accepted outcomes mean "dump written, checksum verified" - BackupOutcome.vb
defines Partial as exactly that, and docs/database-design.md says a dump that
verified but could not copy off-host "is neither" success nor failure.

Why this costs no coverage - a coverage audit of BackupCommandTests, all four
tests:

  Backup_Succeeds_WritesDumpWithChecksumThatVerifies
      subject: dump + size + SHA-256 recomputed against bytes + BackupLogs row
      asserts OffHostPath? NO
  Backup_WithWrongCredentials_ReportsFailureAndNeverClaimsSuccess
      subject: a broken run reports Failed and leaves no artefact behind
      asserts OffHostPath? NO
  Backup_WhenOffHostVolumeAbsent_ReportsPartialNotSucceeded
      subject: the absent-volume branch. Points at label
      "NO-SUCH-VOLUME-<guid>", so it never depended on the environment
      asserts OffHostPath? YES - asserts it is NULL when absent
  Backup_PrunesOldestDumpsBeyondRetentionCount
      subject: retention count
      asserts OffHostPath? NO

No test in this class has ever asserted OffHostPath is non-null or
byte-identical when the volume IS present. That claim rested, and still
rests, on evidence/phase-1/p1-17-backup-success.log - captured 2026-08-22
against the real D: MERCHBACKUP volume, byte-identical copy, checksums
agreeing. Nothing was removed by this change; a hardware dependency was.

Owed at Phase 6, per ADR-019: a real assertion for the volume-present
off-host copy, when plan.md section 7 promotes backup to production quality
with retention and off-host rotation (closing G-15, G-16).


